USER-ADRES package
==================

This package implements the Adaptive Resolution Scheme (AdResS) method for LAMMPS,
enabling hybrid molecular dynamics simulations where molecules can transition
between atomistic (fine-grained) and coarse-grained (CG) resolution regions.

**Note**: The current implementation provides force interpolation between atomistic
and CG pair styles, but does not enforce center-of-mass (COM) constraints for
molecules in the CG region. See LIMITATIONS.md for details.

**Implementation Status**: A comprehensive plan for completing the AdResS implementation
is available. See IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md for the full roadmap.

Contents
--------

The package provides the following commands:

* fix adress/thermo - Applies thermodynamic corrections (thermodynamic force)
* fix adress/region - Manages resolution regions and transitions
* pair adress - Handles hybrid pair interactions
* compute adress/stats - Provides diagnostics and statistics
* fix adress/constraint - COM constraint system (framework exists, implementation in progress)

Installation
------------

This package is installed by default. To include it in your LAMMPS build:

Traditional make:
  make yes-adres

CMake:
  -D PKG_ADRES=on

Authors
-------

This package implements the Adaptive Resolution Scheme (AdResS) method for
hybrid atomistic/coarse-grained molecular dynamics simulations.

